# Proccess of implementing

## Principles

• Always ask clarifing before implemetation
When asking questions: suggested answer build on apps Readme.md; tell what will happen - results
• User must know changes & their effects
• Always write documentation when: 
- Changing what was already documented
- Adding new / removing behavior, functionality...
- Working on app, automation...

### Documentation Requirnments:
- Keep docs laconic - without buzz words
- Always document all important details, main ideas & small implementation specific corners
- If find any differences or not documented things (on truenas, apps...) - document it
- Dont write values in documentation, which stored in `instance/{app}/.env`

## Step 0: Battle user's ideas & goals - suggest better alternatives - research better methods

1. Ask questions, to make sure you 100% understand user's goals
2. Research what will happen
Depending on result of research:
• if this ideas & goals are good ideas → Step 1
• if you thinking its not, tell to a user: why (what can & will happen as result if implement this idea), research better alternatives 

## Step 1: Documentation creation

Goal: Create documentation when 100% clear what user wants & how to implement it

1. Ask questions, to make sure you 100% understand user's goals & how to implement them
2. Create documentation
3. Stop, so user could read documentation

## Step 2: Implementation

Goal: Implement only what according to plan; if something not according to plan: research, analyse, tell user analys & suggest what to do